<section class="intro compact"><h1>Small pieces.<br>Explicit boundaries.</h1><p class="lead">Orku Web is an optional rendering layer, not a new application runtime.</p></section>
<div class="prose"><h2>Trusted templates. Untrusted values.</h2><p>Templates are application-owned PHP code. Dynamic text and quoted attributes use <code>$view->escape()</code>. Links use URL validation. Intentional raw markup requires <code>TrustedHtml</code>.</p><p>Ordinary PHP echo is not automatically escaped. These templates cannot sandbox malicious code.</p><h2>Composition without hidden state</h2><p>Each render receives explicit props and slots. The layout owns this document; the same navigation and footer serve every page. Nested rendering failures discard partial output.</p><h2>Keep the request small</h2><p>No mandatory Node.js, hydration, database or frontend runtime. Read-only pages do not start sessions. The feedback page starts one lazily for its CSRF token.</p><h2>A development milestone</h2><p>Orku Web v0.2 is not a stable release or a production-readiness guarantee. Multipart forms, file uploads, authentication and worker mode are outside this milestone.</p></div>
